  "reputation": {
    "summary": "The bipolar partner to JFET MUSES01 and a premium DIP8 rolling favourite in Japan, China and the West. Japanese blogs praise dynamics, thick mid-bass and resolution; reportedly 'MUSES01 for vocals, MUSES02 for jazz and classical'. Soomal finds it steady but somewhat dull. ASR: the €33 MUSES02 measured only about 0.3 dB quieter than the €5 OPA1656 in a phono stage.",
    "sonic_descriptors": [
      "dynamic",
      "thick, punchy mid-bass",
      "rich, mellow (芳醇)",
      "high resolution",
      "monitor-like thick core",
      "warm, restrained (内敛)",
      "steady but dull (Soomal)"
    ],
    "typical_uses": [
      "Op-amp rolling in DACs and amps (Fosi ZA3/V3 compatible)",
      "FiiO E12A/A5 (+LME49600); X7 AM2 (+BUF634), AM5 (+TPA6120A2)",
      "VentureCraft SoundDroid Vantam front end (or LME49860)",
      "Preamps, active filters and line amplifiers",
      "Upgrade from NJM4580 / NE5532 in Japanese DIY"
    ],
    "caveats": [
      "Counterfeits and remarks are widely reported on marketplaces.",
      "Maintenance product since 2025-03-19: to be discontinued soon, not for new designs. DIP8 only.",
      "100 nA typ (500 nA max) bias: offset rises with high source impedance or DC coupling. Needs ±3.5 V minimum.",
      "Datasheet THD (AV=+10, 5 Vrms, 2 kΩ) is not comparable to LME49860/OPA1612 figures; measured noise edge is small.",
      "Voicing is subjective and polarising; descriptors are listening impressions, not measurements."
    ],
